# .env.example.hdhr — HDHomeRun tuner-emulation env vars (used with docker-compose.hdhr.yml)
# =====================================================================================================
# Append the relevant line(s) to your .env when layering the HDHomeRun override:
#     docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.hdhr.yml up -d

# The reachable LAN IPv4 to advertise in UDP-discovery replies (the tuner's BaseURL / LineupURL). Only has
# an effect when the container can actually RECEIVE the discovery broadcast, i.e. HOST networking or the
# MACVLAN compose. It does NOTHING on plain bridge: Docker bridge never delivers the LAN broadcast into a
# container, so Plex cannot AUTO-discover an emulated tuner on bridge — add it in Plex manually by base URL
# instead (http://<host-LAN-IP>:3000/hdhr/<tunerId>; see docker-compose.hdhr.yml).
# In host/macvlan mode, set this to the host's (host-net) or the container's (macvlan) LAN IP so the
# advertised URLs don't point at an unreachable 172.x container address; leave UNSET on bridge (the HTTP
# serving surface self-corrects its BaseURL from the request Host header regardless).
# MASQ_HDHR_ADVERTISE_HOST=192.168.1.50
